      "side": 1,
      "message": "There was not a bug related to Auto Discharge Disconnect.  This CL was intended to give a clean base to work on.  A number of issues looked like they were related to the way ADD was originally implemented and I wanted to remove that from the code before starting to debug the actual known bugs.  I felt it was more important to do this than fixing the current set of symptoms.\n\nI have copied the CL links into b:151152817 and asked others to test this out.  There are still two remaining issues to call that issue resolved.\n\n1) Initial boot from an already running state performs a hard reset and reboots.  This is probably due to the chip not being in a clean state and should have been power cycled to start clean.\n2) On booting the AP we go into Dual Role Power capable. An open connector will not perform the required initialization that will set this connection correctly so that an attach, at least for a USB Sink device, will not be detected.",
